# Semgrep ignore file. A project file replaces the default list of Semgrep, so the default entries come first and unchanged. Do not edit that block.
#
# Below the defaults only exact files are named: no directory, no glob. They are files that cannot carry an inline suppression comment (stored patches),
# and build recipes that run fixed steps at image build time. Source code takes an inline `nosemgrep` comment with the short rule id and a reason.
# Each entry has `<rule id>: <reason>` in the comment directly above it.

# Administrative folder or file used by popular version control systems
.git
.svn
.hg
_darcs
CVS

# Paths to files and folders that are typically large and ignorable
build/
vendor/
dist/
*.min.js
.env/
.tox/

# Package managers
node_modules/
.npm/
.yarn/
.venv/
_opam/
_build/
_cargo/
# Note that PHP composer uses vendor/ and C++ conan uses build/
# .venv is used both by Go and Python.

# Common test paths
test/
tests/
testsuite/
*_test.go

# Named files. One exact file for each entry.

# generic-api-key: the patch adds a unit test that passes the literal text bedrock-api-key to a mock as a placeholder option, which is no
# credential. The patch is stored byte for byte and pinned by its SHA-256 in engine/cline/lock.toml, so it cannot carry a suppression comment.
engine/cline/patches/0001-feat-llms-route-Bedrock-Mantle-models-through-SigV4-.patch

# aws-access-token: the patch adds a test that holds a made-up example key id, which is no credential. The patch is stored byte for byte and
# pinned by its SHA-256 in engine/cline/lock.toml, so it cannot carry a suppression comment.
engine/cline/patches/0006-fix-cli-never-send-the-ACP-placeholder-key-as-a-bear.patch

# aws-access-token: the test-only export of the same patch, with the same made-up example key id and no credential. It is stored byte for
# byte and pinned by its SHA-256 in engine/cline/lock.toml, so it cannot carry a suppression comment.
engine/cline/patches/tdd/0006-test-only.patch

# set-pipefail, use-workdir: images/worker-python/Dockerfile builds the worker image. The flagged RUN steps change into a fixed directory and
# check a pinned SHA-256 with a pipe that ends in `sha256sum -c`, whose exit code decides the step. They run at image build with fixed
# arguments, never in a running worker.
images/worker-python/Dockerfile

# ifs-tampering: the flagged line declares `local IFS` in retry_run and sets it to the default value, a guard against an inherited IFS and not
# tampering. images/services/install.sh installs the native services at image build with fixed arguments, never in a running worker.
images/services/install.sh

# ifs-tampering: the flagged line declares `local IFS` in retry_run and sets it to the default value, a guard against an inherited IFS and not
# tampering. images/tools/fetch.sh downloads pinned release assets at image build with fixed arguments, never in a running worker.
images/tools/fetch.sh

# detected-aws-account-id: the file is the committed record of one model smoke test and names the account it ran in. An account id is an identifier
# in a data record and no credential, and JSON has no comment form for an inline suppression.
engine/catalog/smoke-us.zai.glm-5.3.json

# detected-aws-account-id: accounts.json is the list of the AWS accounts, profiles, Regions and availability zone ids of the stages. An account id is
# an identifier in a data file and no credential, and JSON has no comment form for an inline suppression.
accounts.json

# dangerous-subprocess-use-audit: scripts/lib/agentd_build.py is a build-time helper (the worker image build, deploy and the fake-engine test step),
# not product runtime logic. It runs cargo, zig and git through argument lists, never a shell. The matching bandit exclude is in .bandit.
scripts/lib/agentd_build.py
